@startuml GupShup Cafe - WebRTC Audio Setup Sequence

' Use latest PlantUML version features
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam participant {
    BackgroundColor #E3F2FD
    BorderColor #1976D2
}

title GupShup Cafe - WebRTC Audio Communication Setup (MVP)

participant "User A\n(Alice)" as Alice
participant "React App A\n(AudioContext)" as ReactA
participant "Socket.io A" as SocketA
participant "AWS Fargate\n(Backend)" as Backend
participant "Socket.io B" as SocketB
participant "React App B\n(AudioContext)" as ReactB
participant "User B\n(Bob)" as Bob
participant "STUN Server" as STUN

== Initialize Audio ==

Alice -> ReactA : Join room
ReactA -> ReactA : AudioContext.initializeAudio()

ReactA -> Alice : Request microphone permission
Alice -> ReactA : Allow microphone

ReactA -> ReactA : navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia()
ReactA -> ReactA : Got localStream (audio only)
ReactA -> ReactA : Apply constraints:\n- echoCancellation: true\n- noiseSuppression: true\n- autoGainControl: true

ReactA -> SocketA : emit('ready-for-webrtc')
SocketA -> Backend : ready-for-webrtc event
Backend --> SocketA : 'webrtc-ready' confirmation

note right of ReactA
    AudioContext now ready
    for peer connections
end note

Bob -> ReactB : Join same room
ReactB -> ReactB : AudioContext.initializeAudio()
ReactB -> Bob : Request microphone permission
Bob -> ReactB : Allow microphone
ReactB -> ReactB : Got localStream

ReactB -> SocketB : emit('ready-for-webrtc')
SocketB -> Backend : ready-for-webrtc event
Backend --> SocketB : 'webrtc-ready' confirmation

== WebRTC Signaling: Create Offer ==

Backend -> Backend : Detect 2 ready participants
Backend --> SocketA : 'create-webrtc-offer'\n{targetPeer: Bob}

ReactA -> ReactA : createPeerConnection(Bob)

note right of ReactA
    RTCPeerConnection config:
    - iceServers: [STUN servers]
    - iceTransportPolicy: 'all'
end note

ReactA -> ReactA : pc = new RTCPeerConnection(config)
ReactA -> ReactA : pc.addTrack(localStream.audio)

ReactA -> ReactA : Setup event handlers:\n- onicecandidate\n- ontrack\n- onconnectionstatechange

ReactA -> ReactA : pc.createOffer()
ReactA -> ReactA : pc.setLocalDescription(offer)

ReactA -> STUN : Gather ICE candidates
STUN --> ReactA : ICE candidates

ReactA -> SocketA : emit('webrtc-offer', {target: Bob, offer})
SocketA -> Backend : webrtc-offer event

Backend -> Backend : Route to target peer
Backend --> SocketB : 'webrtc-offer' {from: Alice, offer}

== WebRTC Signaling: Create Answer ==

ReactB -> ReactB : Got offer from Alice
ReactB -> ReactB : createPeerConnection(Alice)
ReactB -> ReactB : pc = new RTCPeerConnection(config)
ReactB -> ReactB : pc.addTrack(localStream.audio)

ReactB -> ReactB : pc.setRemoteDescription(offer)
ReactB -> ReactB : pc.createAnswer()
ReactB -> ReactB : pc.setLocalDescription(answer)

ReactB -> STUN : Gather ICE candidates
STUN --> ReactB : ICE candidates

ReactB -> SocketB : emit('webrtc-answer', {target: Alice, answer})
SocketB -> Backend : webrtc-answer event
Backend --> SocketA : 'webrtc-answer' {from: Bob, answer}

ReactA -> ReactA : pc.setRemoteDescription(answer)

== ICE Candidate Exchange ==

ReactA -> ReactA : onicecandidate triggered
ReactA -> SocketA : emit('webrtc-ice-candidate', {target: Bob, candidate})
SocketA -> Backend : webrtc-ice-candidate event
Backend --> SocketB : 'webrtc-ice-candidate' {from: Alice, candidate}
ReactB -> ReactB : pc.addIceCandidate(candidate)

ReactB -> ReactB : onicecandidate triggered
ReactB -> SocketB : emit('webrtc-ice-candidate', {target: Alice, candidate})
SocketB -> Backend : webrtc-ice-candidate event
Backend --> SocketA : 'webrtc-ice-candidate' {from: Bob, candidate}
ReactA -> ReactA : pc.addIceCandidate(candidate)

note over ReactA, ReactB
    ICE negotiation continues
    until connection established
end note

== Connection Established ==

ReactA -> ReactA : onconnectionstatechange: 'connected'
ReactA -> ReactA : ontrack: remoteStream received
ReactA -> ReactA : Store remoteStream in Map<peerId, stream>
ReactA -> ReactA : Create <audio> element
ReactA -> ReactA : audio.srcObject = remoteStream
ReactA -> ReactA : audio.play()

ReactA --> Alice : Bob's audio playing

ReactB -> ReactB : onconnectionstatechange: 'connected'
ReactB -> ReactB : ontrack: remoteStream received
ReactB -> ReactB : Store remoteStream in Map<peerId, stream>
ReactB -> ReactB : Create <audio> element
ReactB -> ReactB : audio.srcObject = remoteStream
ReactB -> ReactB : audio.play()

ReactB --> Bob : Alice's audio playing

note over Alice, Bob
    P2P Audio connection established!
    Audio flows directly between peers,
    not through backend.
end note

== Audio Level Monitoring ==

loop Every 100ms
    ReactA -> ReactA : Analyze audio level
    ReactA -> ReactA : AudioContext.getAudioLevel()
    ReactA --> Alice : Display audio bars
end

loop Every 100ms
    ReactB -> ReactB : Analyze audio level
    ReactB -> ReactB : AudioContext.getAudioLevel()
    ReactB --> Bob : Display audio bars
end

== Mute/Unmute ==

Alice -> ReactA : Click mute button
ReactA -> ReactA : AudioContext.toggleMute()
ReactA -> ReactA : localStream.getAudioTracks()[0].enabled = false
ReactA -> SocketA : emit('participant-muted')
SocketA -> Backend : participant-muted event
Backend --> SocketB : 'participant-muted' {peerId: Alice}
ReactB --> Bob : Show Alice as muted

Alice -> ReactA : Click unmute button
ReactA -> ReactA : AudioContext.toggleMute()
ReactA -> ReactA : localStream.getAudioTracks()[0].enabled = true
ReactA -> SocketA : emit('participant-unmuted')
SocketA -> Backend : participant-unmuted event
Backend --> SocketB : 'participant-unmuted' {peerId: Alice}
ReactB --> Bob : Show Alice as unmuted

== Cleanup ==

Alice -> ReactA : Leave room
ReactA -> ReactA : AudioContext.stopAudio()
ReactA -> ReactA : pc.close() for all peers
ReactA -> ReactA : Stop all tracks in localStream
ReactA -> ReactA : Clear remoteStreams Map
ReactA -> SocketA : emit('leave-room')
SocketA -> Backend : leave-room event
Backend --> SocketB : 'participant-left' {peerId: Alice}
ReactB -> ReactB : pc.close() for Alice
ReactB -> ReactB : Remove Alice's audio element
ReactB --> Bob : Alice left the room

note as WebRTCNotes
    **WebRTC Audio Configuration (MVP):**
    
    1. **Codec Priority**: Opus (best for voice)
    2. **STUN Servers**: Google public STUN
    3. **Audio Constraints**:
       - Echo cancellation: ON
       - Noise suppression: ON
       - Auto gain control: ON
    4. **Fallback**: No TURN server in MVP
       (works on most networks)
    
    **Connection Flow**:
    1. Alice & Bob request mic permissions
    2. Backend coordinates signaling
    3. Peers exchange SDP offers/answers
    4. ICE candidates gathered via STUN
    5. P2P audio connection established
    6. Audio flows directly (not via server)
end note

@enduml
